## Micro ledger (inside one SDLC run)

The SDLC run executes in a **separate per-invocation harness** (the [micro dispatch target](#macro-section));
the resident macro agent and that harness share this ledger, so it is a **shared, on-disk,
gitignored** directory — never Hermes `memory` (memory does not cross a harness boundary).

- **Substrate:** {{MICRO_SUBSTRATE}}   <!-- always: shared on-disk (gitignored) -->
- **Ledger root:** `{{LEDGER_ROOT}}`   <!-- e.g. .loom/handoffs/ — gitignored -->
- **Namespace:** `<stage>/<milestone-slug>/…` (human-readable slug, not a timestamp)
- **Manifest:** one row per seam artifact; **latest row for a milestone wins**.

### Seam artifacts per stage

| Stage seam | Producer (writes at exit gate) | Artifacts | Consumer (discovers at entry gate) |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Shaping → Delivery** | Shaping profile | {{SHAPING_ARTIFACTS}} | Planner |
| **Delivery → Closing** | Orchestrator (via Verifier evidence) | {{DELIVERY_ARTIFACTS}} | Closing profile |
| **Closing (final)** | Closing profile | {{CLOSING_ARTIFACTS}} | — (closes the trail) |

Producing the seam artifact is **mandatory at these two stage seams**. Within a stage
(phase-to-phase, dispatcher → utility via `delegate_task`) handoff is advisory.

### The transition (across the altitude seam)

The stage-to-stage transitions above happen **inside the dispatched SDLC harness** against this
shared ledger. The macro agent crosses the seam only twice per leaf: it **PRODUCEs** the entry
`shaping/` artifact when it dispatches a buildable leaf down, and it **DISCOVERs** the exit
`delivery/<milestone>/verified-change` when the run reports back `sdlc:done`. It does not follow the
run through its inner Shaping → Delivery → Closing transitions.

## How to PRODUCE / DISCOVER

- **PRODUCE** (stage exit): compress the session (`stage-handoff` skill), write the stage's expected
  artifacts to the ledger namespace, **reference** PRDs/ADRs/commits by path/URL (never re-embed),
  register a manifest row (status: `ready-for-delivery`, `shipped`, `preserved`, `in-progress`).
- **DISCOVER** (stage entry): read the manifest, find the latest `ready-for-*`/`shipped` row for the
  milestone, load **only** that artifact — keep the session-start context budget small
  (`session-bootstrap` skill).

